# Docker build context excludes. The image builds `gecko` from source INSIDE the
# container (see Dockerfile), so none of the host build/output/asset trees belong
# in the context. Without this file, `COPY . .` uploads the entire working tree —
# dominated by a multi-GB `target/` — as build context (observed: 20GB).

# Rust build artifacts (the big one — rebuilt in-container; never ship host target/)
target/

# VCS + CI + editor cruft
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.githooks/
**/.DS_Store

# Runtime assets — NEVER in the build tree (load-bearing rule #1). Belt-and-suspenders
# in case a cache/index/model was ever staged under the repo.
**/models/
**/*.safetensors
**/*.onnx
**/*.gguf
**/*.bin
**/*.hnsw
.cache/

# SDD scratch ledger (git-ignored) + local scratch
.superpowers/
scratchpad/

# Docs / packaging that the build doesn't need
docs/
README.md
HomebrewFormula/
docker-compose.yml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
